			<div class="content" id="post-content-1336953">
									

<p>It's a generic spider-reptile-like thing that kills you, without even doing it interestingly.</p>
<p>Yet for some reason I like it very much.</p>
<p>Containment Procedures are full of awesome. Sentence &quot;Any researchers present inside of the testing chamber are to remain there during the termination protocol.&quot; captures the very essence of my mental image of the Foundation.</p>
<p>Audio addendum is nice, so are the photos.</p>
<p>Grey Dragon Incident is really really very good.</p>
<p>I think the only thing that bugs me is that they weight exactly 1kg. Kilograms are human-made thing, not nature-made. I would be okay if they weighted exactly A^B*C, where A, B, C correspond to some fundamental constants (or prime numbers, prime numbers are always good), or exactly 1.0268&#160;kg. But making it 1kg bugs me.</p>

							</div>

								
					
